<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-436] Journal#rollLog may leak file handler</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-436</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Just seen the peice of code in Jouranl#rollLog &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; {
                    FileOutputStream fos = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; FileOutputStream(file);
                    fos.write(buff);
                    fos.getChannel().force(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;);
                    fos.close();
                } &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; (IOException e) {
                    LOG.error(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Problems writing to &quot;&lt;/span&gt; + file, e);
                }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On exception It is just logging and continuing.&lt;br/&gt;
Even though FileOutputStream provides finalize implementation and which will clean streams, I don&apos;t think it&apos;s a good idea to depend on it as it will not be garanteed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;cleaning with more care would avoid this.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
